[
  {
    "sha": "842d3ad105a4e18bb204989abbdc87e71be9cebd",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoKkgNoAKDg0MmQzYWQxMDVhNGUxOGJiMjA0OTg5YWJiZGM4N2U3MWJlOWNlYmQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T09:07:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T09:07:54Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(multiaxis): stated rotary axis from the machine line, with a refused disagreement\n\nThe rotary kinds (Rotary Contour, Parallel, Offset) read their rotation\naxis from a statement first: the op's own `stated_axis` direction, else\nthe mounted machine's stated rotary lines (tormach-770mx-microarc4's A\nabout X, millturn's spindle C about Z), each anchored through the\nsetup's work offset origin and judged against the model's faces by the\nfit's own gates (camcraft_motion::multiaxis::axis_stated). A revolve on\nthe stated line generates the very path the free fit reads; a line the\nfaces disagree with refuses by name - never a silent fall back to a\nfree fit when a line was stated, and the radial raster stays locked on\nhelical lobes (the radial drop, the next slice, is its answer). Every\nconsumer reads the stated axis first with today's fit as fallback:\nrotary_axis_of (the sim's chord pass, the first traverse, the post\ngate's struck-steel law), rotary_law, rotary_picks, the revolved bar\nthe centre-cutting audit reads, and the letter door (which answers a\nstated line without a fit). The op param saves in the project file\n(PROJECT_VERSION 78), edits in the property page through\nEditOperationParams, and patches through edit_operation.\n\nRefs #2772\n\nCo-Authored-By: FlamingFireCoding agent session (orchestrated)",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "e57416ec964c77bcb8c90a58f39b002f278905c9",
