      },
      "message": "fix(rotary): judge the stated line in its own frame, step the project to v81  The rework of PR #3674 after mkinney's SAFETY review, seven items:  - the judge's radii are read ABOUT THE STATED LINE (axis_stated), never   off the world origin - a common model/WCS translation no longer   inflates the sagitta budget, and the review's 1 mm mutation behind   +10000 mm now refuses by name (motion tests: moved holds, wrong   lines on all three planes at every translation; app test: the bar   at Y+10000, WCS 10001/10002 refuses, 10000 generates); - the project format steps to v81, a version older readers refuse:   upstream owns v78 (reserved_tools) and a conditional v79 (tip   form), the #2826 held branch numbers its step v80; the v79   tip-form conditional stays and reads natively, its round-trip test   pins the folded order, and the old-reader boundary is tested across   all three rotary kinds; - the merge with origin/main resolved as the union: both the stated   axis and main's path picks live on the rotary variants; - before/after screenshots of the Passes-tab group, on the fork's   pr-screenshots branch; - UI structural tests for the group: labels, enabled state, the   Apply commit and its undo, across the three rotary kinds; - the group's help follows the resolver's order (the machine's stated   line first, the fit only when nothing is stated), with a text   assertion; - the example project regenerated at v81.  Refs #2772\nBREAKING CHANGE: the project format steps to v81; an older reader refuses the file rather than drop a stated rotation axis.",
